    <!--
        iBarter Traditional Chinese (zh-TW, 繁体中文) UI strings.

        x:String is the XAML 2009 intrinsic type (resolves to System.String
        at BAML load time).  The previous build used
        xmlns:system="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib" + <system:String>,
        but mscorlib only exists on .NET Framework; on .NET 10 the
        assembly is renamed to System.Private.CoreLib, so the namespace
        failed at runtime and every {DynamicResource str.X} returned
        null - that's why every menu / button / label was empty in the
        running app.  This is the matching fix to Strings.en-US.xaml.

        Phase 2 keeps the keys identical to en-US so the lookup plumbing
        is exercised identically when the language flips. Real zh-TW
        translations land in Phase 3 once all keys are present in
        Strings.en-US.xaml.
    -->

